WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.920
I think you're going to find this interesting.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:07.789
I've talked to you before about the important
distinction between a TV lawyer and a courtroom

00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:08.940
lawyer.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:15.040
For a while now, we have been referring to
Rudy Giuliani as Donald Trump's television

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.690
lawyer for a long time.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:23.179
He goes on TV and he represents Donald Trump,
but he defends Trump in a way that's different

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:25.480
than what you would see in a courtroom.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.310
Many of the things that a TV lawyer can say
are different than what an actual courtroom

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.449
lawyer would say.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:36.160
You can't make the same claims in front of
a judge that you would potentially be making

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.670
on television.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:42.990
These two worlds collided and exploded in
dramatic fashion this week because it was

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:50.101
announced on Sunday or Monday that Rudy would
be representing Donald Trump in court, in

00:00:50.101 --> 00:00:56.400
court in Pennsylvania in one of these completely
bogus voter fraud cases.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.760
And Rudy Giuliani actually was going to be
expected to behave the way.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:09.380
A courtroom lawyer behaves rather than a television
lawyer, and what's just fascinating about

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:15.870
that is that when Rudy Giuliani was directly
pressed by the judge in Pennsylvania about

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:22.150
whether he is actually alleging that voter
fraud took place, Rudy Giuliani said, I am

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:26.979
not alleging that this is it's so important
to understand this because it's not just Rudy

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:27.979
Giuliani.

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:33.270
This has happened with numerous Trump lawyers
in court in filing these various briefs and

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:38.590
motions and complaints when they've been asked,
are you alleging actual voter fraud?

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.560
They all say no.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:46.580
And it's just perfect because Rudy went in
with all sorts of vague claims that left leaning

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:51.000
counties conspired to hurt Donald Trump will
hold a vote.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.280
What does that actually mean?

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.280
Happened, though?

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:59.350
He went in with claims that absentee voting
was unfairly administered in some counties

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.810
versus others.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:06.790
But when it came down to it, he was asked,
are you alleging fraud in court?

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.170
And Rudy said, no, your honor, we are not.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:15.390
And then he went on to say, well, we believe
the process was fraudulent, which is kind

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.230
of a distinction without a difference.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:22.420
But it's still relevant, Rudy, when put in
front of a judge rather than in front of Judge

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.260
Jeanine Pirro on Fox News, who's just the
TV host in front of an actual judge in a court

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:32.180
of law, he can't actually say we are alleging
specific fraud.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:39.300
Instead, he says, we believe the process was
generally fraudulent and led to, I guess,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.000
what he sees as the wrong results, which is
that Donald Trump lost.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:48.640
This is the final confirmation we needed that
even they know when they alleged fraud took

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:52.989
place in public, they don't really believe
it, or at least they recognize they don't

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:56.880
have the evidence to claim that that's what
took place in front of an actual judge in

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:57.880
a court of law.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.319
Now, Rudy wasn't exactly perfect during the
court appearance.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:05.020
He did stop short of saying we are alleging
fraud because they aren't actually.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:09.070
But he did at one point suggest that some
kind of democratic mafia stole the election

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:10.210
from Joe Biden.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.860
There's no evidence of that whatsoever.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.800
Rudy also apparently committed perjury.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.970
Rudy Giuliani submitted a petition to the
court in which he wrote that he is a member

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:23.560
in good standing of the Washington, D.C.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:29.630
Bar Association, when in reality, Rudy Giuliani
is currently suspended from the D.C. bar because

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:34.170
get this, he didn't pay his dues to the Washington,
D.C. bar.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:39.360
Isn't that just perfect? Trump doesn't pay
his contractors and lawyers worry Trump's

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.940
not going to pay them.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:47.819
And Rudy didn't pay to remain part of the
D.C. bar, which led to him perjuring himself

00:03:47.819 --> 00:03:52.280
when he told the Pennsylvania court that he
was a member in good standing of the D.C.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.280
bar.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.280
Now, that's an aside.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:04:01.709
The question is, if you are not alleging fraud,
why are you here to make general points about

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:02.940
elections?

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:06.739
Because it sure as hell seems like you're
here to try to overturn the results of the

00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:08.489
Pennsylvania election.

00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:13.500
And these lawyers that Donald Trump has working
for him are not going to be able to get past

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:17.329
any judge with a reasonable understanding
of what they're doing.

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:23.500
And so far, that's why everything is getting
thrown out by court after court after court.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:29.500
And by the way, speaking of judges, this is
why the Republican Party has been one hundred

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:33.930
and ten percent focused pedal to the metal
during Donald Trump's presidency on getting

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:38.330
as many loyalists into federal judge positions
as possible.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:43.900
They know that on a lot of issues, the law
is not on their side.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.800
So they prepare to corrupt the law by putting
in place their cronies.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.930
And I hate to admit it, they've succeeded
to a great degree.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.740
I've talked about this before.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.830
Mitch McConnell, I think, is a despicable
guy.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:03.620
If you are a Republican, you see Mitch McConnell
and you recognize this is the guy who has

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:08.130
done an amazing job of installing hundreds
of judges.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:12.121
Oh, I mean, if you go pre Trump, it could
even be maybe it's even over a thousand, I

00:05:12.121 --> 00:05:20.980
don't know, endless judges who are going to
continue ruling in a partizan way, whether

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:24.770
you've got a Democrat or a Republican in the
White House, as we are very quickly going

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:28.020
to see during the first couple of years of
the Joe Biden administration, they have done

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.210
a really good job.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.550
I think they're horrible.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.610
I think these judges are horrible.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:36.290
But if you are them, you have to look at Mitch
McConnell and say this.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.479
This guy has been incredibly successful.

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:43.910
And while the Trump scandals continue to rage,
they keep putting judges in judges.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.330
They didn't even stop during coronavirus.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:51.290
And it is something that we will have to contend
with for a long time in the United States.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:55.330
And listen, if they had gotten more of them
in, you might have actually seen some of these

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:59.360
court cases about supposed voter fraud, a
go in Donald Trump's favor.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:00.370
Maybe some still will.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:02.169
For now, they have not.

